{"id":"00000001794531028633:d649ffb3bd4464539a0d3df81d0d81c1","text":"Owner direction (Nate, 2026-11-13 00:48Z, inbox i-1794530812667-81314-0): asked 'Should One's binding generator emit per-class modules so apps only bundle the iOS classes they use (option 1)?', Nate answered '1' (Yes, do option 1). Notes from p250205 (size owner), INFERRED from reading One origin/main a5008847e7: (1) wire.ts wrapHandle picks the JS wrapper from the registerSDKClass registry with superclass fallback, so if a framework barrel stops registering every class, user code that receives a class it never imported at runtime gets a plainer wrapper; keep one/ios/<Framework> registering everything and move only One's backends (22 files, ~40 symbols) to per-class imports. (2) Frameworks hold ~1000-2250 exports each, so a per-symbol module per export adds thousands of Metro modules for user code that imports a whole framework; group per class with its nested types or measure the overhead. (3) The lazy-first-call fix in this task's body only cuts bytes if the bundler splits the dynamic import; plain Metro still bundles the modules. Lane lead decides the design."}

{"id":"00000001794690713038:a948629976c6219d1a03d717b0f9755e","text":"Option 1 implementation pushed at eb9b6387f8bb46214f9023b59ceecd42e66e520c, draft PR https://github.com/onejs/one/pull/1227; review owner a141509, implementation task t-mwgu6y7v-obj0. Per-class modules plus compatible framework barrels; all 17 actual SDK backends migrated (brief estimated 22), UIKitView has no eager SDK import. Explicit returned-handle wrappers retained for UIKit/Contacts/Network. RAN one-basic dev bundle 13,438,570 -> 9,157,725 bytes (-31.9%); minified production 1,921,080 -> 1,917,662; Brotli q11 341,633 -> 341,122. TESTED 290 facade fingerprint guard, barrel registration/export equality, isolated backend wrapper prototypes and negative control. Native Swift SDK extraction/typechecking and real-device behavior were not run on Linux; normal native prebuild regenerates tables under refreshed identity. Full metrics and limitations recorded in implementation task and PR."}

{"id":"00000001794729842498:021d10bc9888044512ca01f297c24a2f","text":"s255078 post-merge review 2026-11-15 (PR #1227 merged as 4e142a89a9 via #1228; reviewed eb9b6387f8 + follow-up 6a8a4be651 on main): APPROVE, no blocking issues. Verified: (1) split-facade v1+v2 correct — selected-class split with dependency closure never imports _barrel; unknown-binding throw guard; (2) all 15+ Rolldown hook-filter conversions equivalent to in-handler guards or safe-direction (checked each: identity-alias ^\\. covers ../, hermes-compat async-substring edge is a no-op skip, rnCodegen TurboModuleRegistry alternative harmless); (3) nativeTransformCache sound — sha256 key pins compiler/esbuild/swc/oxc versions, atomic temp+rename writes; NOTE babel function options are not part of cache identity (same-project builds unaffected; cross-config staleness only if a function option changes with identical JSON); (4) worklet parse reuse safe — no AST mutation in finders; (5) ios-bindings churn is 100% generation-hash swap bd41a4085->a91e1420, numeric symbol IDs stable (verified all 143k changed lines); (6) #1226 intact on main (intermediate removal was a stale-base artifact, restored by merge 74649b); (7) merge resolutions clean unions, no markers; (8) 6a8a4be651 file-count fix (75k->14.6k) reviewed: selection scan + _barrel fallback correct; NOTE every per-class module imports _protocols (70KB UIKit) — future optimization, not a blocker. Mac validation: generate:check PASS (23.5k decls), one build PASS (290 facades), typecheck PASS, vitest 2610 PASS, swift/events proofs PASS, one-basic + native-features prebuilds PASS with tables regenerated to a91e1420 (UIDevice+battery symbols present), one-basic Release-none confirmed correct (empty link set). xcodebuild consumer compile running on studio-64; result to follow."}
